WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.780 --> 00:00:06.730
Press Secretary Kaili McEnany held her second
press briefing yesterday.

00:00:06.730 --> 00:00:11.430
You might remember that Donald Trump's previous
secretary, press secretary Stephanie Grissom,

00:00:11.430 --> 00:00:16.010
held zero point zero press conferences, press
briefings during her entire time as press

00:00:16.010 --> 00:00:17.010
secretary.

00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:21.110
Kelly McCann and he did one of I believe it
was Friday and she did one yesterday.

00:00:21.110 --> 00:00:25.640
Now, in her first one, she famously pledged
not to lie to the press.

00:00:25.640 --> 00:00:30.130
Then she told four major lies, too, related
to the Russia investigation.

00:00:30.130 --> 00:00:32.899
One related to ventilators and one related
to Michael Flynn.

00:00:32.899 --> 00:00:37.980
So in about three minutes, she broke her pledge
not to lie.

00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:43.530
Yesterday, 12 seconds into the press briefing,
she lied by claiming that the U.S. is doing

00:00:43.530 --> 00:00:46.870
the most testing merely by saying we've done
7 million tests.

00:00:46.870 --> 00:00:50.670
Of course, as you all know, what matters is
per capita in a country of three hundred and

00:00:50.670 --> 00:00:52.120
thirty one million people.

00:00:52.120 --> 00:00:58.579
Now, the last time that we covered her press
briefings, I pointed out the press corps needs

00:00:58.579 --> 00:01:00.440
to ask her about that time.

00:01:00.440 --> 00:01:05.329
She went on Fox News in February and said
Trump will never allow Corona virus to come

00:01:05.329 --> 00:01:07.110
to the United States.

00:01:07.110 --> 00:01:08.990
Here's what she said back in February.

00:01:08.990 --> 00:01:09.990
Absolutely.

00:01:09.990 --> 00:01:11.729
This president will always put America first.

00:01:11.729 --> 00:01:13.450
He will always protect American citizens.

00:01:13.450 --> 00:01:15.960
We will not see diseases like the Corona virus
come here.

00:01:15.960 --> 00:01:17.720
We will not see terrorism come here.

00:01:17.720 --> 00:01:22.420
Isn't that refreshing when contrasting it
with the awful presidency of President Obama?

00:01:22.420 --> 00:01:24.030
Kelly McCann, thank you so much.

00:01:24.030 --> 00:01:25.030
Good to see you.

00:01:25.030 --> 00:01:26.030
Thank you.

00:01:26.030 --> 00:01:27.030
Now to his credit.

00:01:27.030 --> 00:01:32.939
Jeff Mason from Reuters yesterday asked her
about exactly those comments.

00:01:32.939 --> 00:01:34.370
Here is how she handled it.

00:01:34.370 --> 00:01:37.149
She turned to a particular page in her notebook.

00:01:37.149 --> 00:01:39.200
She knew the question might show up.

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:40.530
She was prepared.

00:01:40.530 --> 00:01:41.530
Here's how she addressed it.

00:01:41.530 --> 00:01:45.210
She worked for the campaign and he made a
comment, I believe, on Fox.

00:01:45.210 --> 00:01:50.869
She said President Trump will not allow the
corona virus to come to this country, given

00:01:50.869 --> 00:01:53.140
what has happened since then, obviously.

00:01:53.140 --> 00:01:55.299
Would you like to take that back?

00:01:55.299 --> 00:02:02.229
Well, first, let me note, I was asked a question
on Fox Business about president's travel restrictions.

00:02:02.229 --> 00:02:03.229
I noted.

00:02:03.229 --> 00:02:07.009
What was the intent behind those travel restrictions,
which is we will not see the Corona virus

00:02:07.009 --> 00:02:08.009
come here.

00:02:08.009 --> 00:02:11.599
We will not see terrorism come here, referring
to an earlier set of travel restrictions.

00:02:11.599 --> 00:02:15.760
I guess I would turn the question back on
the media and ask similar questions.

00:02:15.760 --> 00:02:20.650
Does Fox want to take back that they proclaim
that the Corona virus would not be a deadly

00:02:20.650 --> 00:02:21.650
pandemic.

00:02:21.650 --> 00:02:25.620
Does The Washington Post want to take back
that they told Americans to get a grip?

00:02:25.620 --> 00:02:28.709
The flu is bigger than the Corona virus, says
The Washington Post.

00:02:28.709 --> 00:02:33.159
Likewise want to take back that our brains
are causing us to exaggerate the threats of

00:02:33.159 --> 00:02:34.159
the Corona virus.

00:02:34.159 --> 00:02:39.150
Does New York Times want to take back that
fear of the virus, maybe spreading it, spreading

00:02:39.150 --> 00:02:40.810
faster than the virus itself?

00:02:40.810 --> 00:02:45.209
Does NPR want to take back that the flu was
a much bigger threat than the Corona virus?

00:02:45.209 --> 00:02:46.830
And finally, once again, The Washington Post.

00:02:46.830 --> 00:02:51.160
Would they like to take back that the governments
should not respond aggressively to the Corona

00:02:51.160 --> 00:02:52.160
virus?

00:02:52.160 --> 00:02:56.750
I'll leave you with those questions and maybe
you'll have some answers in a few days, not

00:02:56.750 --> 00:02:59.939
just your about your.

00:02:59.939 --> 00:03:06.830
What's so funny about this is that she clearly
feels like that was a huge mike drop moment

00:03:06.830 --> 00:03:10.690
where she walks off after turning it back
around on the press.

00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:14.480
It's actually cringeworthy and the entire
thing was cringe worthy.

00:03:14.480 --> 00:03:18.050
She may not last long because it's it's getting
more and more embarrassing.

00:03:18.050 --> 00:03:20.349
Now, the trumpets seem to be liking it.

00:03:20.349 --> 00:03:22.430
That's what might keep her in the job.

00:03:22.430 --> 00:03:25.349
She starts the briefing 35 minutes late.

00:03:25.349 --> 00:03:30.130
It lasts only 25 minutes total after taking
only a few questions.

00:03:30.130 --> 00:03:36.159
She abruptly walks off after being asked about
a completely laughable, ridiculous thing that

00:03:36.159 --> 00:03:37.159
she said.

00:03:37.159 --> 00:03:38.159
But the Trump is love it.

00:03:38.159 --> 00:03:43.430
Donald Trump, Don Junior, tweeted yesterday,
saying her answer was fire.

00:03:43.430 --> 00:03:46.700
And a whole bunch of Trump ists are just thrilled
with Kaylie Malkin.

00:03:46.700 --> 00:03:48.510
So let's analyze her argument.

00:03:48.510 --> 00:03:52.220
She said Trump won't let Corona virus come
to the United States.

00:03:52.220 --> 00:03:57.019
And she responds by saying, listen, a lot
of media outlets said this is not going to

00:03:57.019 --> 00:03:58.909
be a big deal in the United States.

00:03:58.909 --> 00:04:00.640
That's a terrible argument, number one.

00:04:00.640 --> 00:04:01.790
It's not really an argument.

00:04:01.790 --> 00:04:03.719
It's actually the two quick way.

00:04:03.719 --> 00:04:09.410
The fallacy, which is the appeal to hypocrisy,
is another way to say it, which is when you

00:04:09.410 --> 00:04:14.410
tried to discredit your opponent's argument
about something you did by pointing out that

00:04:14.410 --> 00:04:16.209
someone else did the same.

00:04:16.209 --> 00:04:17.870
Thing and it's it's fallacious.

00:04:17.870 --> 00:04:23.520
Strictly speaking, how can the media criticize
her when they said similar things supposedly

00:04:23.520 --> 00:04:25.070
is the way the argument goes.

00:04:25.070 --> 00:04:32.210
Now, first of all, when the media was saying
this may not be a big deal in the United States,

00:04:32.210 --> 00:04:37.360
the media was reporting what different medical
experts were saying.

00:04:37.360 --> 00:04:41.139
Many of whom were people that were involved
with the Trump administration.

00:04:41.139 --> 00:04:46.720
And so so one thing to understand is a lot
of the articles she's quoting are articles

00:04:46.720 --> 00:04:52.889
that are essentially citing the medical experts
that the Trump administration picked for,

00:04:52.889 --> 00:04:54.620
say, things about coronavirus.

00:04:54.620 --> 00:04:55.620
That's number one.

00:04:55.620 --> 00:04:58.169
It's not like the media reports.

00:04:58.169 --> 00:05:02.800
When you look at independent and foreign experts
were not saying this would be a big deal.

00:05:02.800 --> 00:05:07.440
In fact, you can look at January and February
and find a whole bunch of media reports that

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:11.590
are not based on what Trump affiliated medical
experts were saying.

00:05:11.590 --> 00:05:14.751
If you look at foreign countries, if you look
at independent agencies in the U.S., they

00:05:14.751 --> 00:05:18.340
were saying we could take actions that would
prevent this.

00:05:18.340 --> 00:05:20.270
But if we don't, it's going to be a disaster.

00:05:20.270 --> 00:05:22.949
So she's she's actually wrong about that.

00:05:22.949 --> 00:05:27.810
And a lot of the reports that she cites were
simply saying, here's what someone associated

00:05:27.810 --> 00:05:30.180
with the administration says is going to happen.

00:05:30.180 --> 00:05:32.070
She didn't say.

00:05:32.070 --> 00:05:34.350
Here's what an expert says.

00:05:34.350 --> 00:05:38.610
She simply said Trump won't allow the virus
to come here.

00:05:38.610 --> 00:05:43.509
So she made a very different type of claim
when she went on Fox News and said Obama's

00:05:43.509 --> 00:05:45.340
presidency was awful.

00:05:45.340 --> 00:05:46.800
Trump's not going to allow it to come here.

00:05:46.800 --> 00:05:47.910
That was not.

00:05:47.910 --> 00:05:50.139
These are the medical experts alleging that.

00:05:50.139 --> 00:05:54.910
Now, secondly, none of those media people
who were simply reporting what was being said

00:05:54.910 --> 00:05:56.789
were hired to be Trump's press secretary.

00:05:56.789 --> 00:05:57.789
Right.

00:05:57.789 --> 00:06:02.979
The question about her competence is a very
valid and good question, because she was hired

00:06:02.979 --> 00:06:08.419
to be Trump's press secretary, some vox writer
who quoted a health expert who may have been

00:06:08.419 --> 00:06:10.870
wrong or may have been taken out or whatever.

00:06:10.870 --> 00:06:12.979
They are not now speaking for the president.

00:06:12.979 --> 00:06:15.930
But clearly what she has done is show her
hand.

00:06:15.930 --> 00:06:18.569
She is very much willing to attack the media.

00:06:18.569 --> 00:06:22.740
She is prepared to attack the media whenever
she gets the questions she doesn't like very

00:06:22.740 --> 00:06:24.669
much like Donald Trump does.

00:06:24.669 --> 00:06:26.000
That's what we've done.

